      "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\n\nFixes #10498\n\n`CosineReward.cosfn` computes `cos(t * pi / T)`, where `t` is the summed completion length and `T` is `cosine_max_len`. Cosine is periodic, so once `t > T` the reward wraps around. A correct two-turn answer of 2048 tokens (with `T = 1024`) gets +1.0, the same as an empty answer. `SoftOverlong` keeps going below -1 for long completions, while DAPO bounds the penalty to [-1, 0].\n\nThe change clamps `t` to `T` in `cosfn` and the `SoftOverlong` reward to -1.0. Completions at or below the limits score as before.\n\n## Experiment results\n\nRun in a Linux container (CPU only).\n\n- Script from the issue: on main, the correct 2048-token answer scores +1.0 and `SoftOverlong` gives -5.0 at 2048 tokens and -9.0 at 3072 (exit 1). With the fix the correct answer scores +0.5, the same as at 1024 tokens, and `SoftOverlong` stays at -1.0 (exit 0).\n- A sweep over lengths 0 to 3T for T in {8, 64, 512, 1024, 4096}: on main, every step past T breaks the documented monotonic ordering. With the fix, none do.\n- 6,300 generated inputs checked against the documented behaviour of both rewards, with no mismatches.\n\nPre-commit was not run.\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [ ] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [x] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [ ] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n\n\nThis pr was prepared with AI assistance and reviewed by a human.\n",
